207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This method uses the quenching phenomenon of oxygen to calculate the level of DO. Fluorescence from a fluorescent material excited by light from a blue light-emitting diode \(LED\) is quenched by oxygen passed through a DO permeable layer. The higher the DO level is, the stronger the quenching phenomenon is and the less fluorescence the detector \(light-receiving diodes\) detects.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
